'''DEN Networks Limited''' is an Indian [[cable television]] and [[broadband]] service provider company in India. It is owned by Sameer Manchanda and was acquired by [[Reliance Industries]] in 2018 along with [[Hathway]].<ref name=":0">{{Cite web|last=Kapoor|first=Mudit|date=23 October 2018|title=Reliance acquires 58.92% stake in Den Networks, 51.34% share in Hathway|url=https://www.businesstoday.in/top-story/reliance-acquires-58.92-stake-in-den-networks-51.34-share-in-hathway/story/286130.html|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181023133306/https://www.businesstoday.in/top-story/reliance-acquires-58.92-stake-in-den-networks-51.34-share-in-hathway/story/286130.html |archive-date=23 October 2018 |access-date=2021-01-15|website=[[Business Today (India)|Business Today]]}}</ref> In 2003, it stood as one of the three major cable distributors in India alongside Hathway and InCablenet.<ref name=":3">{{Cite book|last=Kohli-Khandekar|first=Vanita|title=The Indian Media Business|publisher=[[SAGE Publications]]|year=2003|isbn=978-0-7619-9650-7|location=|pages=67|language=en}}</ref>

On 17 October 2018, Reliance Industries announced that it had acquired a 66% stake in DEN for {{INRConvert|2290|c}}.{{Citation needed|date=April 2025}} At the time of the acquisition, DEN had 106,000 broadband subscribers.<ref name=":0" /><ref>{{cite web |author1=Reliance |title=Reliance Media Release |url=http://www.ril.com/getattachment/30b9a86d-eb92-4ac6-8a20-62fbbdef58b2/RIL-announces-strategic-investment-in-and-partners.aspx/idcplg?IdcService=GET_FILE&dDocName=APRODCT000702&RevisionSelectionMethod=Latest&Rendition=primary |website=ril.com |access-date=11 Jan 2019 |format=PDF |date=17 October 2018 |archive-date=11 January 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190111175635/http://www.ril.com/getattachment/30b9a86d-eb92-4ac6-8a20-62fbbdef58b2/RIL-announces-strategic-investment-in-and-partners.aspx/idcplg?IdcService=GET_FILE&dDocName=APRODCT000702&RevisionSelectionMethod=Latest&Rendition=primary |url-status=dead }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=Kundu |first1=Rhik |title=What Hathway and Den deals mean for Reliance Jio |url=https://www.livemint.com/Companies/CbIho0Mzxon95xTKoUh2EL/What-Hathway-and-Den-deals-mean-for-Reliance-Jio.html |website=Mint |access-date=7 April 2019 |language=en |date=19 October 2018}}</ref> The acquisition received approval from the [[Competition Commission of India]] in January 2019.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Laghate |first1=Gaurav |title=Reliance Industries gets CCI nod to acquire Hathway, DEN |url=https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/reliance-industries-gets-cci-nod-to-acquire-hathway-den/articleshow/67643807.cms |website=The Economic Times |access-date=7 April 2019 |date=22 January 2019}}</ref> Reliance acquired an additional 12.05% stake in DEN in March 2019 taking its total stake in the company to 78.62%.<ref>{{cite web |title=Reliance Jio acquires another 12% of Den Networks |url=http://www.indiantelevision.com/cable-tv/multi-system-operators/reliance-jio-acquires-another-12-of-den-networks-190309 |website=Indian Television Dot Com |access-date=7 April 2019 |language=en |date=9 March 2019}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Reliance increases shareholding in DEN, Hathway, GTPL through open offer |url=https://www.televisionpost.com/reliance-increases-shareholding-in-den-hathway-gtpl-through-open-offer/ |website=TelevisionPost |access-date=7 April 2019 |date=11 March 2019 |archive-date=7 April 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190407031211/https://www.televisionpost.com/reliance-increases-shareholding-in-den-hathway-gtpl-through-open-offer/ |url-status=dead }}</ref>

